%% @fig 01
%% @kicker Three memory layers
%% @alt The HyperAgent loop reads its working context on every model call. When a session ends, the working context is summarized into episodic memory in a durable store, and the agent queries a long-term knowledge base for facts, procedures, and preferences it doesn't need in every prompt. Each layer down trades speed for capacity.
%% @caption Like registers, RAM, and disk: the agent reaches for a slower layer only when the faster one can't hold the answer.
